  </svg>
</section>

<!-- TIME DIFFERENCE MECHANICS -->
<section class="method-section" id="time-difference" aria-labelledby="time-diff-heading">
  <div class="method-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Mathematical Mechanics</p>
    <h2 id="time-diff-heading">Understanding the +9 Hour Gap</h2>
    <p>
      The relationship between Greenwich Mean Time (UTC+0) and Korea Standard Time (UTC+9) is defined by an exact addition of 9 hours. Because South Korea maintains a single permanent time zone without daylight saving adjustments, this offset remains constant all year round relative to UTC.
    </p>
    <p>
      When it is 6:00 AM GMT in London, local clocks in Seoul show 3:00 PM KST on the same day. When GMT reaches 3:00 PM, Seoul enters midnight (12:00 AM KST) on the next calendar day.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin: 2rem auto; max-width: 700px; padding: 1.5rem; background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 12px;">
    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 600 180" width="100%" height="auto" style="display: block;">
      <rect width="600" height="180" fill="#0c354a" rx="8" />
      <g transform="translate(120, 90)">
        <circle cx="0" cy="0" r="50" fill="#12455d" stroke="#2f6278" stroke-width="3" />
        <line x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="-30" stroke="#f4fbff" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" />
        <line x1="0" y1="0" x2="20" y2="0" stroke="#8fd7ff" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" />
        <text x="0" y="70" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-weight="bold" font-size="14" fill="#f4fbff" text-anchor="middle">GMT (UTC+0)</text>
      </g>
      <g transform="translate(300, 90)">
        <text x="0" y="8" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-weight="bold" font-size="28" fill="#36c7b5" text-anchor="middle">→</text>
        <rect x="-45" y="-30" width="90" height="24" rx="12" fill="#1b536e" />
        <text x="0" y="-14" font-family="'Manrope', sans-serif" font-size="11" font-weight="800" fill="#36c7b5" text-anchor="middle">+9 HOURS</text>
      </g>
      <g transform="translate(480, 90)">
        <circle cx="0" cy="0" r="50" fill="#12455d" stroke="#36c7b5" stroke-width="3" />
        <line x1="0" y1="0" x2="20" y2="12" stroke="#f4fbff" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" />
        <line x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="-30" stroke="#36c7b5" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" />
        <text x="0" y="70" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-weight="bold" font-size="14" fill="#f4fbff" text-anchor="middle">KST (UTC+9)</text>
      </g>
    </svg>
  </div>

  <div class="method-grid">
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>Fixed UTC Standard</h3>
      <p>KST is permanently fixed at UTC+9. There are no seasonal clock adjustments, simplifying server cron jobs and automated schedules.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>Day-Line Crossover</h3>
      <p>Any GMT timestamp after 3:00 PM (15:00 GMT) lands on the following calendar day in South Korea. Always verify the target date.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>European Morning / Korean Evening Overlap</h3>
      <p>The standard business overlap occurs between 8:00 AM and 10:00 AM GMT, matching 5:00 PM to 7:00 PM KST in South Korea.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 24-HOUR CONVERSION TABLE -->
