  <ul style="line-height: 1.8; color: var(--muted);">
    <li><strong style="color: var(--text);">Confusing GMT with British Summer Time (BST):</strong> In summer, London switches to BST (UTC+1), which narrows the gap to Korea to 8 hours instead of 9. Always verify whether your UK baseline is GMT (UTC+0) or BST (UTC+1).</li>
    <li><strong style="color: var(--text);">Forgetting Next-Day Date Roll-Over:</strong> Any GMT event after 3:00 PM (15:00 GMT) lands on the following calendar day in South Korea. Failing to increment the date leads to missed meetings.</li>
    <li><strong style="color: var(--text);">Assuming South Korea Shifts Clocks:</strong> South Korea does NOT observe DST. Do not add or subtract extra hours for summer in Seoul.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

